Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 02:28:23 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 51/51] k27: the single-volume layout only: launchd and APFS
 mount the volumes, the union layout's code goes

The root is the System volume DroidVMSystem of the Data store's APFS container, in the Data volume's volume group, as on a Mac.
launchd's mount-phase-1/2 (apfs_boot_util) mount VM, Preboot, Update, xART, Hardware and Data, and APFS stitches the firmlinks stored
on the System volume (docs/k27-real-disk-layout-plan.md). Verified: mount lists the seven volumes as on a Mac, / and the firmlinked
/Users, /Library, /private/var have the Data volume's device, '..' of a firmlink target is the source's parent, fseventsd, mds,
kernelmanagerd, WindowServer and loginwindow run.

- native_owner_cache_prepare only checks the read-only verified APFS root and publishes the boot manifest of the root alone
  (native_owner_publish_boot_manifest loses its cache volume); nothing is mounted over the root
- gone with the union layout of the OS and SystemOS images:
  - the SystemOS union mount, native_owner_systemos_volume_uuid, native_verified_block_volume_device, native_ram_block_volume_seed
    and vm_unix.c's never-enabled owner cache carrier
  - the kernel's Data mount (native_owner_data_prepare), its firmlinks (native_owner_firmlinks_prepare, the lookup that followed
    them, vfs_flags hiding MNT_UNION on the root) and the gpu-addon and staged-apps bindfs unions after it, with bindfs's boot
    mount exception
  - union-hide-lower: the covering mount's device id and MNT_ROOTFS in stat, statfs, getattrlist and the vfs sysctls, the lower
    mount left out of getfsstat, the hidden Preboot directory
  - the union lookup and getattrlistbulk fixes for the SystemOS union over /
  kpi_vfs.c, vfs_attrlist.c, vfs_lookup.c, vfs_vnops.c and bindfs are xnu's again; CONFIG_FIRMLINKS stays (APFS's firmlinks)
